# Navigation & Shells

## Purpose

Keep one navigation model and guarantee authenticated UI is always wired for notifications/FCM.

## When Applied

Editing routing, post-login destinations, or member/admin shells.

## Requirements

- Imperative `Navigator` + `MaterialPageRoute` only — no go_router/auto_route.
- Enter authenticated member/admin UI **only** through `AuthenticatedShell` (`role == 'admin'` → admin, else member bottom nav).
- Keep `NotificationBloc` + FCM wired via the shell.
- See [`docs/auth-and-roles.md`](../../../docs/auth-and-roles.md) for the role split.

## Examples

```dart
Navigator.push(context, MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => const BookingDetailsPage()));
```

## Anti-patterns

- Routing straight to `AdminHomeScreen`/member home post-login, skipping the shell.
- Introducing a router package or removing `navigation_bloc.dart` unprompted.

## Common Mistakes

- A new post-login path that bypasses notification/FCM setup.
- Mixing declarative routing into the imperative stack.
